course: dictionary
lesson: 3334
title: Everywhere
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Everywhere means in every place, or to every place. When you read it, ask yourself: is the writer talking about one place, or about all of them? «I looked everywhere for my keys» means I searched every place I could think of.
explain: The words around it give you clues. «Germs are everywhere, so we wash our hands» tells you germs are in every place around us, not just in one dirty corner. That is why washing matters.
explain: Stories use everywhere to paint a picture of a whole scene. «There was snow everywhere» means the snow covered the whole place, not just one patch of ground.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «in every place» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Everywhere means in every place or to every place.
fact: «Everywhere you go» means in any place you go.
fact: «Sardine tins everywhere» means sardine tins scattered all over the place.
fact: «Made headlines everywhere» means the news was reported in all places, not just one.
fact: Everywhere is mainly an adverb, a word that tells you where something happens.
exercise: «I looked everywhere for my keys.» What does everywhere mean here? | Very quickly | *In all the places I could think of | Only at school | In just one place, the kitchen
exercise: «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, with sardine tins everywhere.» What does everywhere mean here? | *Scattered all over the place | Kept in the cart | Hidden under the cart | Packed neatly in one box
exercise: «You meet algorithms everywhere.» What does everywhere mean here? | *In every place, from recipes to sat navs | Only inside computers | In one kitchen only
test: «Germs are everywhere, so we wash our hands.» What does everywhere mean? | Only in dirty places | Far away in space | *In every place around us | Under the sink
test: What does «Everywhere you go» mean? | *In any place you go | Only at the seaside | Once a week | In the next town only
exam: The Mona Lisa «made headlines everywhere» after it was stolen in 1911. What does everywhere mean here? | *In every place, so people in all places heard about it | In only one town | Quietly in a museum | In a painting
